Date: Sat, 6 Jun 2026 11:52:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/31] fix(verimark): set enroll_date on list() prints
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Continuation of the fprintd NULL-field crash hunt. fprintd's
`delete_enrolled_fingers` (called at enroll start when an existing
print is found for the same finger) logs the print's metadata via
`g_warning ("Error deleting print from device: %s", err->message)`
plus other diagnostics that touch every FpPrint field. Backfill
the enroll-date too — a NULL GDate trips the same strlen-on-NULL
fault as the username/description fields fixed earlier.

The synthetic date is today; the value is purely a display hint, not
identity. fprintd overrides it when the print is loaded from disk
after a real enroll.

Drafted with AI assistance.
---
 libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
index 4f28662..d879f3e 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
@@ -45,6 +45,7 @@
 #include <gusb.h>
 #include <gio/gio.h>
 #include <string.h>
+#include <time.h>
 
 
 struct _FpiDeviceVerimark {
@@ -1406,6 +1407,15 @@ verimark_print_from_tuid(FpDevice *device,
     fp_print_set_username(print, "verimark");
     fp_print_set_description(print, "Kensington VeriMark DT (device-side enrollment)");
     fp_print_set_finger(print, FP_FINGER_UNKNOWN);
+    /* fprintd logs the enroll-date too — a NULL GDate trips the same
+     * strlen-on-NULL crash. Use today's date as a synthetic stamp ;
+     * the value is only used as a display hint, not as identity. */
+    {
+        GDate *today = g_date_new();
+        g_date_set_time_t(today, time(NULL));
+        fp_print_set_enroll_date(print, today);
+        g_date_free(today);
+    }
 
     return print;
 }
